  <item>
    <title>Hannah Dustin - Don&#039;t mess with her!</title>
    <link>https://hobobiker-prep.ddev.site/hannah_dustin_dont_mess_with_her</link>
    <description>&lt;p&gt;These New Englanders are crazy about their history, of course. Every village has a marker about its own Revolutionary General. Yesterday we rode through Dunbarton, the hometown of &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.seacoastnh.com/framers/stark.html&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;General John Stark,&lt;/a&gt; an admirable man indeed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But today we passed a memorial to &lt;a href=&quot;http://kingsley.locke.net/gen/dustin/hannah.htm&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;Hannah Dustin&lt;/a&gt;. Hannah was carried away by Indians and taken to an island. But with her 10-year-old compatriot, she killed all the Indians, scalped them, and escaped back to home ground. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don&#039;t mess with Hannah Dustin!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
